// Bell material — **pulsing moved into the vertex shader**. The old way of the CPU touching bell.scale ① scaled the whole bell
// uniformly, so it read as 'inflating a balloon', and ② the core couldn't move with it, so it was split off as a separate mesh
// (3 draw calls per individual). Weighting by aBend (top 0 → lip 1) gives a real medusa contraction where **the lip closes first**,
// and the core can be merged into the same geometry and pulsed weakly → 2 draw calls per individual.
