            // more than v → drawing an isotropic granule would need a **0.4px-wide** ellipse in the texture, which is impossible
            // (measured: granules vanished at the arm tips leaving only stripes). The 5 arms are identical, so **fold one arm sector
            // into** u: u=0 arm axis · u=1 valley between arms. 10× resolution, anisotropy 6.3× → 1.6×.
            // Cost: the pattern repeats per arm and mirrors left/right (anything that must exist 'only once', like the madreporite, can't go in).
            const a = (th / (Math.PI * 0.4)) % 1;
