// is a **tubular** loft sweeping a section along an axis, hence fcTubeGeo — different skeletons, don't merge them.
// Both are "closed surfaces sweeping a section along an axis". Factored out as shared like the shells' fcValveGeo — the remaining
// shrimp body and octopus head use it as-is too.
// Rule: **bumps and lumps aren't attached but made with disp (radius displacement)** → the silhouette itself gets bumpy
// and draw calls stay 1. Attached spheres look floating or half-sunk in the silhouette (the old sea cucumber/sea squirt did).
//   rad(s) : section radius multiplier. Must be **0 at s=0·1** so both ends close to poles.
//   sec(ph, s) : section unit direction {x, y} — deformations like a D shape (flat sole) go here
