// to read as a neck, yet too bumpy to be a smooth egg, leaving only a **horizontal crease (step)**. That was why it
// looked like a barrel/mushroom cap (user report). A value that failed both ways.
// v2 discipline: ① head~mantle is **one smooth egg** — no bumps in the middle
//          ② the neck pinch goes **deep just above the arm roots (s 0.10~0.22)** — that's the real neck
// Common reference principle: "a large, rounded oval for the head (mantle)".
// v3: s=0 (the very bottom) **pinched in** to 0.40, looking like a small saucer sitting on the arm crown —
// the cause of the visible step between head and arms (user report "이어진 부분 이상해" — the joint looks wrong).
// Leave the bottom open **at the arm-root thickness (0.52)** and put the neck pinch just above it at s 0.12.
